### Library Management API - Books & Catalog
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### Login as Librarian first to obtain auth token
# @name loginLibrarian
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "librarian@library.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

@librarianToken = {{loginLibrarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1. List / Search Books (Public - All titles, sorted by title)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?page=0&size=10&sort=title,asc

### 2. Search Books by Keyword (e.g. 'clean' or 'java')
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?query=clean&page=0&size=10

### 3. Filter Only Available Books
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?availableOnly=true

### 4. Get Book by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/b1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### 5. Create a New Book (Librarian)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{librarianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "9780135957059",
  "title": "The Pragmatic Programmer: 20th Anniversary Edition",
  "description": "Your journey to mastery in software development.",
  "publicationYear": 2019,
  "language": "English",
  "categoryId": "c1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "authorIds": [
    "a2222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222"
  ],
  "totalCopies": 3
}

### 6. List All Categories (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories

### 7. Create a Category (Librarian)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{librarianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cloud Computing & DevOps"
}

### 8. List All Authors (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/authors?page=0&size=20

### 9. Create an Author (Librarian)
POST {{baseUrl}}/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{librarianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Andy Hunt"
}
